<title>DUBAI: Iran puts Q1 oil revenues at $4.1 billion.</title>
<headline>Iran puts Q1 oil revenues at $4.1 billion.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-07-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>OPEC heavyweight Iran said on Saturday its oil exports during the first quarter of the Iranian year (March 21-June 21) fetched $4.1 billion.</p>
<p>The official IRNA news agency quoted Iran's vice petroleum minister for trade Ghanimi Fard as saying that Iran has achieved 96 percent of oil export revenue forecast for the period.</p>
<p>He said the average export price during the period was $17 per barrel.</p>
<p>Iran ranks after Saudi Arabia and Norway as the world's largest crude exporter with an OPEC quota of 3.6 million barrels per day.</p>
</text>
